{"ok":true,"provider":"openai","model":"gpt-5.6-sol","actualModel":null,"output":"{\"verdict\":\"fail\"}\n\nLane E1 found false shipped claims. The strongest failures are execution-proven: the enforcer converts unknown/unreadable checks into `status:\"ok\"` with exit 0; the audit exceeds its disclosed lexer ceiling; the enforcer is not wired into any standing gate; several hook descriptions overstate their mechanisms; the residual register is incomplete under its own derivation rule; and multiple debt rows describe code that no longer exists at the pin.\n\nOutside-read keys used below:\n\n- `C`: complete reads of `gate-failclosed-audit.js` L1-698, its test L1-292, `gate-failclosed-enforcer.js` L1-248, its test L1-197, registry L1-239, and baseline L1-93.\n- `W`: standing-wiring search across settings, `/scan:full`, hooks, release gates, testsuite, recurring-class registry, and `.github`; relevant callers were then read directly.\n- `H`: complete reads of all seven repaired hooks, settings hook order, `scripts/deps/admission.js`, and `scripts/hooks/lib/project-config.js`.\n- `R`: complete residual register L1-90, debt-snapshot L303-375, relevant commit history and branch refs.\n- `L`: complete debt-snapshot L303-375 plus the exact mechanism regions cited by each row.\n\nFalse current claims\n\n1. `gate-failclosed-audit.js:23-25` — “handler body can reach … a `{ ok: true, ... }`-shaped return” — false. This requires the object return to be reachable. Valid JavaScript `return\\n{ok:true}` returns `undefined` through automatic semicolon insertion, but `analyzeSource()` reported `success-shaped return`. Outside=`C`; execution-proven.\n\n2. `gate-failclosed-audit.js:116-120` — code inside template interpolation “is left intact so brace matching and keyword search operate on real code only” — false. A valid catch containing `` `${/}/.test(\"}\") ? process.exit(0) : 1}` `` was not matched, while `` `${/process.exit(0)/.test(\"x\")}` `` produced a false finding from regex text. The interpolation loop has no regex state. Outside=`C`; execution-proven.\n\n3. `gate-failclosed-audit.js:117-120` — “newlines preserved for line-number accuracy” — false for JavaScript line terminators other than LF. CR, U+2028, and U+2029 findings were reported on line 1; a `//` comment terminated by CR swallowed a real `process.exit(0)` completely. Outside=`C`; execution-proven.\n\n4. `gate-failclosed-audit.js:64-67` — “No bare count anywhere without the emitted list it derives from” — false. The audit emits `files_scanned` without the scanned-file set; the enforcer likewise emits baseline, registry, repaired, and untriaged counts without their exhaustive member sets. Outside=`C`; execution-proven and reasoned.\n\n5. `gate-failclosed-enforcer.js:12-15` and registry L5 — a site is decision-dependent gate syntax, “exactly what … analyzeSource() finds” — false granularity. The audit only recognizes permissive-shaped syntax and performs no gate-decision analysis. Its tool-correlated set includes the explicitly `not-a-gate` rows `{edit-watcher.js catch/statement 674/675, edit-watcher.js catch/statement 897/898}`. Outside=`C`; reasoned from full files.\n\n6. `gate-failclosed-enforcer.js:29-32,95-98` — the live audit has a nested-try blind spot and structurally cannot reach the seeded nested sites — false. `gate-failclosed-audit.js:398-411` removed the skip-ahead, and executing the nested fixture found both outcomes at lines `{15,20}`. Outside=`C`; execution-proven.\n\n7. `gate-failclosed-enforcer.js:7,24-40,196-215` — “Blocks FORWARD” through the stated nonzero failure modes — false for could-not-check paths. With a nonexistent `--root`, the audit condition was zero readable files plus ENOENT, but the enforcer printed `status:\"ok\"`, `live_files_scanned:0`, and exited 0. With a nonexistent `--base-dir`, all repaired-row reads failed, but it again exited 0. Outside=`C`; execution-proven.\n\n8. `gate-failclosed-enforcer.js:207` — `checked_repaired_count:7` — false f