ith the configured warn-mode runner path observed exiting 0.\n\n21. `worktree-preflight.js:7,110-115` — it cleans orphan worktrees/branches and prints `Cleaned …` — false. `git()` swallows every failure into `\"\"`; deletion attempts are appended to `cleaned` regardless, and the directory-removal fallback catch is unreachable through that helper. Outside=`H`; reasoned; this mutating hook was deliberately not executed.\n\n22. `worktree-preflight.js:8,136-143` — it blocks when no smoke test ran “this session” — false unit. It checks only existence of a persistent marker with no session identifier, timestamp validation, or bound writer. Marker existence does not prove a test or a session; absence proves only no marker. Outside=`H`; reasoned.\n\n23. `worktree-preflight.js:161-165` — orphan-cleanup git errors reach the outer catch — false because L25-32 swallows them. Consequently L157’s “infra checks passed” can be emitted after failed cleanup or failed stale-branch enumeration. Outside=`H`; reasoned.\n\n24. `S6-7-RESIDUALS.md:35` — status, N, K, and ceiling are all reported — false and internally contradicted by its own final clause. The enforcer emits N/K but drops audit status and ceiling. Outside=`R`; execution-proven.\n\n25. `S6-7-RESIDUALS.md:13-19,90` — completeness is bounded only by the derivation rule — false closure. No exhaustive source population is emitted, and the confirmed pre-assembly omitted set is `{ED-374 amendment L312, ED-381 L309/L316, ED-383 L311/L313, ED-396 L337/L339}`. Each was open, predated assembly, named an unclosed/out-of-fence gap, and explicitly traveled under S6-7 or the successor-enforcer route. Outside=`R`; reasoned from emitted records and commit timestamps.\n\n26. `S6-7-RESIDUALS.md:81-82` — nothing records prompt SHA/bytes and dispatch wall-clock — false across the stated dispatch population. Subprocess records already carry `{started_at, prompt_bytes, prompt_digest}` in `dispatch-agent.js:1088-1113` and `dispatch-claude.js:759-78